Organic edible oils are derived from plants through natural cultivation methods that exclude synthetic pesticides, herbicides, and genetically modified organisms (GMOs). The oils retain higher levels of naturally occurring nutrients, antioxidants, and essential fatty acids, offering a healthier alternative to conventional oils. Common varieties include canola, soybean, olive, palm, peanut, and coconut oils, each produced under strict organic certification standards.
