What is Organic Edible Oil?
Organic edible oil refers to any vegetable derived oil that is produced in compliance with internationally recognized organic farming regulations. The production process emphasizes soil health, biodiversity, and the avoidance of synthetic agro chemicals. As a result, the final oil is free from chemical residues, exhibits superior oxidative stability, and delivers enhanced nutritional profiles such as higher omega 3 fatty acids in cold pressed canola or elevated polyphenol content in organic olive oil.
